---
layout: null
sitemap: false
---
{%- comment -%}
  Built by Jekyll, not by a script, straight from the results pages' front
  matter — so it is correct on every deploy without anyone remembering to
  re-run anything.

  race.html renders the "Earlier This Cycle" panel from
  assets/data/race-results-index.json, which bakes each election's status in at
  the time that index was last generated. That index is rebuilt when results
  change; a certification is often just a status flip with byte-identical
  numbers, so it can be flipped on the results pages and in the archive and
  still leave race.html saying "Unofficial" for a certified election — which is
  exactly what happened to the June 16 primary runoff. This file is the live
  overlay race.html applies on top of the baked index.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign stubs = site.pages | where: 'layout', 'election_results' | sort: 'election_date' -%}
{
  "metadata": {
    "source": "Results page front matter, resolved against the counted votes",
    "vocabulary": ["upcoming", "unofficial", "certified"],
    "count": {{ stubs | size }}
  },
  "elections": {
    {%- for stub in stubs -%}
    {%- include result-status.html stub=stub -%}
    {{ stub.results_data | jsonify }}: {
      "status": {{ result_status | jsonify }},
      "mode": {{ stub.results_mode | default: 'round' | jsonify }},
      "advances": {{ stub.runoff_advances | default: 2 }},
      "date": {{ stub.election_date | date: "%Y-%m-%d" | jsonify }},
      "url": {{ stub.url | jsonify }},
      "updated": {{ stub.updated | date: "%Y-%m-%d" | jsonify }}
    }{% unless forloop.last %},{% endunless %}
    {%- endfor %}
  }
}
